## `useQuery`

The `useQuery` hook is used to fetch data from a GraphQL server. It takes two arguments:

1. A GraphQL query string, which can be either a [document](https://graphql.org/learn/queries/#document-notation) or a [request string](https://graphql.org/learn/queries/#request-string).
2. An object containing the variables to pass along with your request.

The hook returns an object that contains three properties:

1. `data`: The data returned by the GraphQL server.
2. `loading`: A boolean indicating whether the query is currently being fetched from the server.
3. `error`: An error message if there was a problem fetching the data.

```tsx
// app/products/index.tsx
import { useQuery } from 'react-apollo';

export default function Products() {
  const { loading, error, data } = useQuery(
    gql`
      query products($limit: Int!) {
        products(limit: $limit) {
          id
          name
        }
      }
    `,
    { variables: { limit: 10 } },
  );

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>{error.message}</div>;

  const { products } = data;

  return (
    <>
      {products.map(product => (
        <Product key={product.id} {...product} />
      ))}
    </>
  );
}
```

