## Authentication with NextAuth.js

NextAuth.js is a complete authentication solution that works out of the box and can be used to authenticate users in your app. It handles user registration, login/logout, password reset, account verification, social sign-in (Google, Facebook, Twitter) and more.

### Install NextAuth.js

```bash
npm install next-auth-example
```

### Configure NextAuth.js

NextAuth.js is configured in `pages/_app.tsx`. It uses the [Session API](https://nextjs.org/docs/api-reference/next/session) to store authentication state and handles user login, logout and account verification.

```ts
// app/pages/_app.tsx
import { SessionProvider } from 'next-auth'
import { authConfig } from '@/auth'

export default function App({ Component }) {
  return (
    <SessionProvider session={session}>
      <Component />
    </SessionProvider>
  )
}
```

### Configure Authentication Routes

NextAuth.js uses [pages](https://nextjs.org/docs/basic-features/pages) to handle authentication routes. These are the routes that require authentication and are protected by NextAuth.js.

```ts
// app/pages/login.tsx
import { signIn } from 'next-auth'

export default function LoginPage()  {
  return <button onClick={() => signIn('google')}>Login with Google</button>
}
```

